<div class="section-en" lang="en" style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <h2>Scientific Appeal: Why the Rescue of Nature is Inseparably Linked to the Social State and Peace</h2>
    
    <h3>I. The Realistic Solution: Social State and Reform</h3>
    <p>Humanity no longer has a single second to lose on utopian theories or abstract discourses that do not correspond to today's realities. In a world full of crises, there is <strong>no other realistic solution than the social state</strong> to push back structural fascism, stop institutional exploitation, and actively protect human dignity. It is a vital necessity to defend the social state as a fortress against cuts and to develop it sustainably through radical reforms. The rescue of civilization and nature depends on the success of this real reform movement.</p>

    <h3>II. Call to Scientists and Intellectuals: The Anti-Fascist Front</h3>
    <p>We appeal to all thinkers, scientists, and sociologists worldwide: Knowledge must not be in the service of palaces, capital, or militarism. Fascism and world war threaten to wipe out more than half of humanity and the ecological system. Against this threat, a <strong>natural anti-fascist front</strong> must be established, uniting world politics and science. Intellectuals must scientifically expose those control structures originating from slavery, in which religious and civil institutions with huge budgets systematically exploit the sick and helpless under the guise of care. Silence means complicity in this increase of the fascistic dose. Science must urgently erect a rational peace barricade.</p>

    <h3>III. Preventing War: Nature- and Human-Centered World Politics</h3>
    <p>The rush for attack-oriented rearmament is a fascistic mechanism directly programmed to destroy the very foundations of life. This voice from Germany demands a fundamental turnaround. Either we distance ourselves from aggressive global militarism, or we stop this destructive course through a worldwide grassroots movement.</p>

    <p>We demand the following concrete steps for the future:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Departure from abstract ideologies:</strong> The social state must be strengthened worldwide through radical reforms as the only concrete solution.</li>
        <li><strong>Formation of the anti-fascist front:</strong> Scientists must immediately organize an alliance that exposes institutional exploitation.</li>
        <li><strong>Stop the attack transformation:</strong> Rüstung budgets must be cut and shifted into social security and ecological protection.</li>
    </ul>

